{"id":"Prowl.Runtime.NavMeshObstacle","name":"NavMeshObstacle","display":"NavMeshObstacle","kind":"class","assembly":"Prowl.Runtime","namespace":"Prowl.Runtime","outer":null,"signature":"public class NavMeshObstacle : Component","bases":[{"name":"Component","id":"Prowl.Runtime.Component"}],"docs":{"summary":"Blocks agents while enabled — a parked vehicle, a dropped crate, a placed building.\n\n[`Carve`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.NavMeshObstacle~Carve) on cuts a hole in the navmesh so pathfinding routes around it; the affected tiles rebuild over the following frames, and with [`CarveOnlyStationary`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.NavMeshObstacle~CarveOnlyStationary) the hole lifts while moving and re-applies once still for [`CarvingTimeToStationary`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.NavMeshObstacle~CarvingTimeToStationary). Carving runs in the editor too, so placing a building shows the hole it will cut.\n\n[`Carve`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.NavMeshObstacle~Carve) off is velocity-obstacle mode: the mesh is untouched and the obstacle joins each crowd as an immovable neighbour, so agents steer around it locally. Free to move, but paths are computed as if it weren't there, so an agent with no other route presses against it.\n\nEither way the object's own geometry stays out of bakes — voxelizing it would freeze a hole where it happened to be standing."},"attributes":["AddComponentMenu","ComponentIcon","ExecuteAlways"],"members":[{"kind":"property","name":"Shape","signature":"public NavMeshObstacleShape Shape { get; set; }","docs":{},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":69,"path":"Prowl.Runtime/Components/Navigation/NavMeshObstacle.cs","anchor":"Shape"},{"kind":"property","name":"Center","signature":"public Float3 Center { get; set; }","docs":{},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":70,"path":"Prowl.Runtime/Components/Navigation/NavMeshObstacle.cs","anchor":"Center"},{"kind":"property","name":"Size","signature":"public Float3 Size { get; set; }","docs":{},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":71,"path":"Pr